{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774736,"nonce":"zkKAE/R6aXyRF3qtJe9H492+WVM=","title":"feat(settings): global Settings shell + org-scoped secrets (ADR-0060 slice 1)","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #74 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `feat/adr-0060-settings-org-secrets` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-25T16:42:32Z · Merged: 2026-07-25T17:30:23Z\n\nFirst slice of ADR-0060. Closes git-bug `d2cee7d`.\n\nOrg secrets are the base of the `env → repo → org` inheritance chain, and\n`/v1/secrets` has always accepted the org scope — but **no UI reached it**,\nso setting one meant raw HTTP. There was nowhere to put the surface: every\nexisting screen hangs off a repo, and org config has no repo.\n\n- **`/settings`** — a new top-level route, holding its first section: **Org\n  Secrets** (full CRUD at org scope). No org switcher, no org navigation:\n  there is exactly one Org (single-tenant *experience*), but `Org` stays the\n  model's real RBAC / secret inheritance root (ADR-0049 / ADR-0037) rather\n  than being collapsed away.\n- **`GET /v1/me` gains `can_administer` + `admin_orgs`** — the UI can't hide\n  an entry it can't evaluate, and offering a door that 403s is worse than\n  offering none.\n- **A gear in the topbar**, rendered only for admins, plus a palette entry\n  under the same condition.\n- **`ScopedSecrets`** — the secrets panel extracted out of `RepoView`,\n  scope-agnostic, so the repo tab and Settings render *one* component at\n  two scopes instead of drifting apart.\n- **`session.ts`** — `/v1/me` fetched once for the whole app, so the avatar,\n  the gear and the palette can't disagree mid-render.\n\nWhat does **not** grant org settings: a **Project**-scoped `Administer`.\nAdministering one repo is not administering the org (ADR-0049 — Org inherits\ndown, never up). Both halves are asserted — the repo admin sees no gear\n*and* gets a 403 if they hit the endpoint directly.\n\n`admin_orgs` is empty on a fresh install: an org exists only as the\ncoordinate of a bound Project (there is no `orgs` table, ADR-0046).\n`can_administer` still reads true there, because Settings is exactly where\nthe first connection gets added in slice 3.\n\n- `crates/scarab-server/tests/org_settings.rs` — 5 feature-acceptance tests:\n  org reported and deduplicated across Projects · fresh install can\n  administer with no org yet · org-scoped Admin does full secret CRUD and\n  never sees a value · **Project admin is refused, nav *and* API** · Viewer\n  gets nothing\n- `cargo test -p scarab-server` green; `npm test` 72 passed; typecheck +\n  build clean\n- Driven in mock mode (`VITE_SCARAB_MOCK=1`): `/settings` lists the\n  org-scope keys, the repo Secrets tab still lists its own after the\n  extraction, gear lights only on its own route\n\nSlice 2 (`af1ffae`, editable matrix) is stacked on this branch; slice 3\n(`998f20b`, `/v1/connections`) adds the second Settings section.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}